    <!-- Education articles -->
    <string name="article_skinprint_title">Understanding Your SkinPrint™</string>
    <string name="article_skinprint_summary">How Camera, Probe, your answers and AI come together into one evolving picture.</string>
    <string name="article_skinprint_body">Your SkinPrint™ blends four inputs: what the camera observes, what the probe measures, the context you shared, and the goals you set. Each contributes a piece to a single, evolving picture of your skin — never a diagnosis, always a starting point for tracking change over time.</string>
    <string name="article_skin_basics_title">Skin Basics: Getting Oriented</string>
    <string name="article_skin_basics_summary">A gentle primer on how skin works and why everyone\'s baseline looks different.</string>
    <string name="article_skin_basics_body">Skin is a living, changing organ shaped by genetics, environment and habits. There\'s no single \"normal\" — what matters is understanding your own baseline and noticing how it shifts over time, not comparing it to anyone else\'s.</string>
    <string name="article_understanding_skin_title">Understanding Your Skin Type</string>
    <string name="article_understanding_skin_summary">Why skin type and sensitivity are starting points, not fixed labels.</string>
    <string name="article_understanding_skin_body">Skin type and sensitivity can shift with season, stress and routine changes. Treat your self-reported profile as a helpful starting point, and revisit it if your skin\'s behavior changes.</string>
    <string name="article_ingredients_title">Reading Ingredient Labels with Confidence</string>
    <string name="article_ingredients_summary">What to look for when a product\'s ingredient list feels overwhelming.</string>
    <string name="article_ingredients_body">Ingredient lists are ordered by concentration. Rather than chasing trends, focus on what a product is meant to do for your routine — cleanse, hydrate, protect or target — and introduce new ingredients one at a time.</string>
    <string name="article_daily_habits_title">Small Habits, Meaningful Signals</string>
    <string name="article_daily_habits_summary">How sleep, stress and sun exposure show up in your skin over time.</string>
    <string name="article_daily_habits_body">Daily habits like sleep quality, hydration and sun exposure don\'t change your skin overnight, but they compound. Tracking them alongside your routine can help you notice patterns worth adjusting.</string>
    <string name="article_routines_title">Building a Routine That Sticks</string>
    <string name="article_routines_summary">Why a simple, consistent routine usually outperforms a complicated one.</string>
    <string name="article_routines_body">The most effective routine is the one you\'ll actually follow. Start with the essentials — cleanse, protect and one targeted step — and build from there only if it earns its place.</string>

